A raise inside a called function unwinds to the handler that resolved it, as
the host's own exception does. The body of a handler whose raises the checker
resolved to a boundary is one catch block (passErrorCatch), so the raise ends
the handler; a call statement carrying a per-call @error is caught at that call
(catchAtCall), and the handler goes on after it.

So `age = parseTwice("")` under the boundary stops in requireAge, passes back
through parseTwice without reaching `return n * 2`, leaves `age` as it was and
skips `problem = "saved"`; the boundary's handler runs in its place. The
per-call handler on `requireAge` catches there instead, and `age = 0` after it
still runs. Before, a raise in a call whose value is used was caught nowhere,
and a raise that did reach the boundary ran its handler and let the click go
on.

The argument case is the third button: a per-call handler answers for its own
call, and `string(requireAge(""))` is evaluated before that call is made, so it
is bound to a temp ahead of the statement and its raise reaches the boundary.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `e := ErrorEvent\{` -- no raise inlines its handler any more; each one panics to a recover
deny out/none/html/index.html `let e = \{ message: "` -- nor in JavaScript
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `throw RuntimeException` -- a raise throws SnglRaise, which is what the catch names

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

func requireAge(s string) int {
    if s.length == 0 {
        error.raise("an age is required", "validation")
    }
    return int(s)
}

func parseTwice(s string) int {
    var n = requireAge(s)
    return n * 2
}

component form() node {
    var problem = "none"
    var age = 7
    vbox {
        boundary(@error(e) {
            problem = e.message
        }) {
            button(text="Save", @click {
                age = parseTwice("")
                problem = "saved"
            })
            button(text="Check", @click {
                requireAge("", @error(e) {
                    problem = "call: " + e.kind
                })
                age = 0
            })
            button(text="Argument", @click {
                parseTwice(string(requireAge("")), @error(e) {
                    problem = "not this one"
                })
            })
        }
        text(value="problem={problem} age={age}")
    }
}

window #home(title="raise") {
    form()
}

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}
